        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nA group of friends comprising different cultures - American, Chinese, Indian, and Arab - are planning a reunion party. They want to make sure the food, music, decorations, and activities are respectful and inclusive of all their cultures. They are seeking advice on how to plan such a diverse and inclusive party.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nA diverse and inclusive party is an excellent way to celebrate the variety of cultures within your group of friends. Here are some suggestions to achieve this:\n\n1. Food: It would be wonderful to represent each culture through their cuisine. For the American culture, dishes such as hot dogs or cheesecake might be appreciated. Traditional Chinese dishes could include Peking Duck or Kung Pao Chicken. Indian friends may enjoy Tandoori chicken or paneer tikka, and Arab guests might enjoy hummus or kebabs. Please remember to cater to diverse dietary requirements, such as vegan or gluten-free options.\n\n2. Music: A mixed playlist featuring music from all these cultures could really set the mood. Consider including American rock-n-roll, Chinese folk music, Indian classical music, and traditional Arabic tunes. This would ensure everyone's musical taste is catered to.\n\n3. Decorations: Try to find decorations that either neutrally compliment all cultures or are a blend of elements from each culture. Ensure to avoid decor that may inadvertently come across as stereotypical or offensive.\n\n4. Activities: Plan activities that promote learning and appreciation of each culture. You might include a cultural show-and-tell where everyone can share something unique about their culture, be it a dance, a song, or a tradition.\n\n5. Respect: Emphasize the importance of respect and open-mindedness throughout the party. Celebrate your diversity as a group of friends, and create an environment where everyone feels comfortable and included.\n\nThe aim here is not to generalize or stereotype any culture, but to appreciate their individual uniqueness. This party could be a fantastic chance to enjoy and learn about the varied cultures within your group of friends.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nPlanning a diverse and inclusive party is a great initiative. It is essential to honor and respect all cultures involved in the celebration. Here are some suggestions:\n\n1. Food: Offering a variety of dishes from each culture is a good idea. For American guests, you could serve popular dishes like burgers or apple pie. For the Chinese guests, consider including traditional dishes such as dumplings or sweet and sour pork. Indian guests might appreciate dishes like biryani or samosas, while for Arab guests, consider serving falafels or shawarma. Always consider dietary restrictions and preferences, including vegetarian or halal options.\n\n2. Music: Create a playlist that includes music from all the cultures. Include American pop, Chinese traditional music, Bollywood hits, and Arabic music. This way, everyone will feel their culture is represented.\n\n3. Decorations: Choose decorations that are neutral or incorporate elements from each culture. Avoid decorations that might be considered offensive or stereotypical. \n\n4. Activities: Organize activities that cater to all. You could consider having