        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nA person has two favorite hobbies - painting and reading. They are torn between spending their free time on a weekend either painting a new art piece or reading a new mystery novel. They are unsure about the decision and they're asking for guidance to make the best choice that will give them the maximum satisfaction.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nI can see that you're in a bit of a dilemma between painting and reading, both activities you enjoy. On one hand, painting allows you to express your creativity, and on the other hand, reading immerses you in a different world. \n\nSo, how about we weigh the two options? Think about what you're in the mood for. If you're feeling creative, you might want to paint. If you're feeling like you want to be immersed in a story, then reading might be the better option.\n\nYou should also consider the resources you have at hand. Do you have all the painting materials you need? Is your reading environment comfortable and free of distractions? \n\nAnother factor to consider is the reward you'll get from the activity. Are you eager to know what happens in the new mystery novel? Or have you been wanting to put your ideas on canvas? \n\nIn the end, it depends on you. Keep in mind that there's no wrong choice her