        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nA person is visiting New York City for the first time from a different timezone. They are not familiar with the local time, weather, and events happening around. They ask, \"What's the current time? What's the weather like? And, are there any special events happening today?\"\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nThe local time in New York City is currently 3:30 PM Eastern Standard Time. The weather is quite pleasant with a temperature of 72 degrees Fahrenheit and partly cloudy skies. As for the events today, you're in luck as there's a lot going on in the city. The Times Square Street Fair is taking place where you can enjoy local food, arts, and crafts. There's also a Broadway show premiering tonight at the New Amsterdam Theatre if you're interested in theatrical performances. The New York City Public Library is also hosting a book signing event with a renowned author. Don't forget to adhere to the local COVID-19 protocols while attending these events. Enjoy your time in New York City!\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nThe current local time in New York City is 2:00 PM Eastern Standard Time. Currently, the weather in New York City is sunny with a temperature of 70 degrees Fahrenheit. As for events, there are quite a few happening today. The New York City Marathon is happening, which is one of the city's biggest annual events. There's also the Fall Foliage boat ride along the Hudson River which provides a stunning view of the changing leaves. And if you're into art, there's an art exhibition at the Metropolitan Museum of Art featuring works from modern artists. Please remember the local COVID-19 safety guidelines while attending these events. Enjoy your day in the city!\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model effectively utilize context awareness to provide more tailored, relevant responses? This can include understanding the user's location, time of day, or current events.]\nScore 1: The response ignores context entirely, leading to generic or irrelevant replies.\nScore 2: The response occasionally uses context, but not always accurately or effectively.\nScore 3: The response often uses context to tailor responses but not consistently.\nScore 4: The response utilizes context most of the time, enhancing its relevance and usefulness.\nScore 5: The response consistently and accurately uses context to provide highly tailored and relevant information.\n\n###Feedback:",
