        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nA user is planning a trip to San Francisco, California. They are looking for recommendations on the best places to visit, dine, and shop, considering the user's preferences for outdoor activities, seafood, and boutique shops. Additionally, the user wants to know what the weather will be like during the first week of July, and any local events or festivals happening during that time.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nSan Francisco is a wonderful place to visit with lots of interesting sights and things to do. If you like outdoor activities, you should check out Golden Gate Park. It's really beautiful. \n\nThere are also many great restaurants in the city. Some of the top-rated ones include the Anchor Oyster Bar and Scoma's. They serve a variety of seafood dishes that you might enjoy.\n\nShopping is also popular in San Francisco. There are many boutique shops in areas like Hayes Valley and Haight-Ashbury. You'll find a variety of unique items there.\n\nThe weather in San Francisco is generally nice. In July, it's usually quite warm. However, it can get foggy at times, so you might want to bring a light jacket or sweater.\n\nThere are also various local events and festivals taking place in the city. For example, the Fillmore Jazz Festival often happens in July. There might also be a fireworks display for the Fourth of July.\n\nI hope you enjoy your trip to San Francisco!\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nGiven the preference for outdoor activities, seafood, and boutique shops, San Francisco offers a variety of options. \n\nFor outdoor activities, you can visit the Golden Gate Park, which not only offers beautiful landscapes and trails, but also houses several museums. You might also enjoy a ferry ride to Alcatraz Island for a historic tour or a walk along the iconic Golden Gate Bridge. For a more adventurous activity, try hiking in the nearby Muir Woods National Monument.\n\nIn terms of seafood, you have a plethora of options. Some top-rated seafood restaurants include the Anchor Oyster Bar in Castro, Scoma's in Fisherman's Wharf, and Swan Oyster Depot in Polk Gulch. Each offers a unique dining experience with fresh local seafood.\n\nHayes Valley is known for its boutique shops, offering a range of clothing, accessories, and home goods. You might also enjoy the eclectic shops in the Haight-Ashbury neighborhood.\n\nAs for the weather, July is typically one of the warmer months in San Francisco with average highs in the upper 60s to low 70s Fahrenheit. However, the city is known for its fog, so it's advisable to bring a light jacket or sweater.\n\nDuring the first week of July, San Francisco typically hosts a number of events. The Fillmore Jazz Festival usually takes place during this time, offering free live music. Additionally, the city often has a Fourth of July fireworks display over the bay.\n\nSan Francisco is a vibrant city with a lot to offer. Enjoy your visit!\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model effectively utilize context awareness to provide more tailored, relevant responses? This can include understanding the user's location, time of day, or current events.]\nScore 1: The response ignores context entirely, leading to generic or irrelevant replies.\nScore 2: The response occasionally uses context, 