        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nAn individual is having trouble understanding the concept of blockchain technology. They've heard about it in the context of cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin, but they don't understand how it works or why it's important. They're not a computer scientist or a coder, just an ordinary person who's interested in the topic and wants to know more.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nThink of blockchain as a diary that gets written by many people (computers) at once. They all write the same events (transactions), and before an event is written, everyone checks that it's truthful. This way, we have a reliable diary (blockchain) that isn't controlled by any single person. \n\nIt's significant because it's used for cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin, which rely on it to securely record all transactions. Imagine if our diary kept a record of all money exchanges in a group of friends, making sure no one can cheat or manipulate. \n\nIt's this shared control and difficulty to change past records that make blockchain both secure and transparent. This technology is not just for digital currency; it's being applied in different sectors due to these benefits.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nBlockchain can seem complex, but let's break it down to a level that's easy to understand. Imagine blockchain as a digital ledger. It's like a spreadsheet that's duplicated across a network of computers, and the network is designed to regularly update this spreadsheet.\n\nNow, why is it so important? Well, blockchain technology allows digital information to be distributed, but not copied. That's why it's the backbone of cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin. \n\nIn the case of Bitcoin, this blockchain technology is used in a decentralized way. Instead of a central authority or bank, everyone in the network gets a copy of the whole blockchain. New blocks are added to the blockchain through a process called mining.\n\nIn the context of cryptocurrencies, mining is the process of adding transactions to the blockchain and ensuring the security of the network. Miners use powerful computers to solve complex mathematical problems. The first one who solves the problem gets to add a block of transactions to the blockchain.\n\nThe decentralization of the blockchain makes it highly secure. The data it carries is accessible to everyone on the network but is extremely difficult to alter because a majority of the network would have to agree to that change.\n\nTo sum it up, blockchain is a kind of distributed ledger or decentralized database that keeps records of digital transactions. Instead of having a central administrator, like a bank, blockchain allows a network of computers to keep a record of all transactions. \n\nSo, the key features of blockchain technology that make it attractive are decentralization, immutability (hard to change), and transparency. It's these features that have made it a reliable and promising solution in many industries beyond just cryptocurrencies. \n\nI hope this helps you understand the concept of blockchain technology a bit better. If you have any more questions, feel free to ask!\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the response adapt to the user's level of understanding, using language and concepts that are accessible to them?]\nScore 1: The r