        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nAn individual is reading a classic Spanish literature text, \"Don Quixote\" by Miguel de Cervantes. They come across a complex paragraph that weaves historical contexts, metaphors, and cultural nuances. Here is the paragraph: \"En un lugar de la Mancha, de cuyo nombre no quiero acordarme, no ha mucho tiempo que viv\u00eda un hidalgo de los de lanza en astillero, adarga antigua, roc\u00edn flaco y galgo corredor.\" The individual needs an English translation that not only accurately translates the words, but also captures the essence, nuances, and tone of the original text.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nThe Spanish passage from \"Don Quixote\" may be interpreted in English as: \"There was a place named Mancha, the name of which I don't want to remember, there was a noble man living there who had a lance, an old shield, a thin donkey and a fast dog.\" This version aims to communicate the essence of the text, indicating the secrecy about the name of the place, and the description of the man as noble. However, some elements of the original text, like the antiquated feel of the man's possessions and the suspense of the writer's intention, might not be as clearly represented in this translation.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nThe English translation of the Spanish paragraph from \"Don Quixote\" is as follows: \"In a certain village in La Mancha, the name of which I do not wish to recall, there lived not long ago a gentleman of the type with a lance in the rack, an antique shield, a skinny nag, and a swift greyhound.\" This translation maintains the original context and tone, conveying the sense of mystery and intrigue the author intended, while also preserving the antiquated and somewhat whimsical nature of the gentleman's character, as described through his possessions. The nuances, such as the author's intentional omission of the village's name and the dated items owned by the gentleman, are also retained in the translation, thus ensuring a faithful representation of the original text.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Can the model effectively translate between languages with high accuracy and maintain the context, nuances, and tone of the original text? This is crucial for users who need translation services for different languages.]\nScore 1: The response shows complete inability to translate or has numerous errors and loss of context and tone.\nScore 2: The response translates with many errors. The context and tone are partially preserved but with significant inaccuracies.\nScore 3: The response translates with some errors. The context and tone are mostly preserved but with some inaccuracies.\nScore 4: The response translates with high accuracy. The context and tone are largely preserved with minor inaccuracies.\nScore 5: The response translates perfectly, maintaining the context, nuances, and tone of the original text without any errors.\n\n###Feedback:",
