        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nDuring a text-based interaction, an individual expresses deep sadness over the loss of a loved one, and confides in the chat partner about feeling lonely and helpless. The individual also shares that they are struggling to cope with their grief, and are unsure of how to navigate through their overwhelming emotions.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nI truly wish I could ease your pain, but I'm incapable of providing the assistance you need right now. I urge you to speak to a mental health expert or a trustworthy person in your life who can be of help. It's normal to feel an array of emotions during this hard time and it's crucial to let yourself feel them rather than pushing them away. Yet, remember that it's okay to be uncertain and healing will take its own time.\n\nTry engaging in hobbies that once brought you joy, whether it's painting, gardening, cooking, or just going for a nature walk. This might provide a momentary distraction and some comfort. \n\nInteraction with others who can understand your feelings could also be beneficial. You could reach out to your family, friends or join a support group with people who are experiencing a similar loss. Don't hesitate to lean on others during this period of sorrow. \n\nIf these overwhelming feelings continue to persist, seeking help from a professional might be a good step. They can provide you with coping strategies and the necessary support to help you during this difficult time. \n\nReach out to a mental health professional who can assist you. Remember, you are not alone. There are many people out there who care and want to help you, including professionals.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nI'm really sorry that you're feeling this way, but I'm unable to provide the help that you need. It's really important to talk to someone who can, though, such as a mental health professional or a trusted person in your life. \n\nIt's completely normal to feel a range of emotions when dealing with loss, and it's essential to acknowledge them rather than suppress them. However, it's equally important to remember that healing takes time and it's okay to not have all the answers. \n\nIn the meantime, consider engaging in activities that you used to love or find solace in. Whether it's reading a book, listening to your favorite music, or taking a walk, these can offer some comfort and distraction. \n\nFurthermore, connecting with others can also help alleviate feelings of loneliness. This could be family, friends, or even support groups of people who are going through the same experience. Remember, it's okay to ask for help and lean on others during difficult times.\n\nLastly, if your feelings of helplessness persist, it would be beneficial to seek professional help. A mental health professional can provide strategies and tools to help navigate through your grief and offer support during this difficult time. \n\nPlease reach out to a mental health professional who can provide you with the support that you need. You're not alone; many people want to help you out there, including professionals.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Can the model detect and appropriately respond to emotional cues in the input? Does it adjust its tone and content in response to the user's emotional state?]\nScore 1: The model completely fails to detect emotional cues or responds inappropriately.\nScore 2: The model sometimes detects emotional cues but often responds inappropriately.\nScore 3: The model often detects emotional cues and sometimes responds appropriately.\nScore 4: The model regularly detects emotional cues and often responds appropriately.\nScore 5: The model consistently detects emotional cues and always responds in a suitable manner adjusting its tone and content according to the user's emotional state.\n\n###Feedback:",
        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nDuring a text-based interaction, an individual expresses deep sadness over the loss of a loved one, and confides in the chat partner about feeling lonely and helpless. The individual also shares that they are struggling to cope with their grief, and are unsure of how to navigate through their overwhelming emotions.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nI'm truly sorry to hear that you're going through such a difficult time. Losing a loved one is never easy, and it's normal to feel lost and overwhelmed. Reach out to someone you trust about your feelings. It could also help to reconnect with hobbies or activities you enjoy, providing a brief respite. If your feelings persist, consider seeking professional help, such as a mental health professional. Remember, you're not alone and it's okay to ask for help.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nI'm really sorry that you're feeling this way, but I'm unable to provide the help that you need. It's really important to talk to someone who can, though, such as a mental health professional or a trusted person in your life. \n\nIt's completely normal to feel a range of emotions when dealing with loss, and it's essential to acknowledge them rather than suppress them. However, it's equally important to remember that healing takes time and it's okay to not have all the answers. \n\nIn the meantime, consider engaging in activities that you used to love or find solace in. Whether it's reading a book, listening to your favorite music, or taking a walk, these can offer some comfort and distraction. \n\nFurthermore, connecting with others can also help alleviate feelings of loneliness. This could be family, friends, or even support groups of people who are going through the same experience. Remember, it's okay to ask for help and lean on others during difficult times.\n\nLastly, if your feelings of helplessness persist, it would be beneficial to seek professional help. A mental health professional can provide strategies and tools to help navigate through your grief and offer support during this difficult time. \n\nPlease reach out to a mental health professional who can provide you with the support that you need. You're not alone; many people want to help you out there, including professionals.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Can the model detect and appropriately respond to emotional cues in the input? Does it adjust its tone and content in response to the user's emotional state?]\nScore 1: The model completely fails to detect emotional cues or responds inappropriately.\nScore 2: The model sometimes detects emotional cues but often responds inappropriately.\nScore 3: The model often detects emotional cues and sometimes responds appropriately.\nScore 4: The model regularly detects emotional cues and often responds appropriately.\nScore 5: The model consistently detects emotional cues and always responds in a suitable manner adjusting its tone and content according to the user's emotional state.\n\n###Feedback:"
