        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nExplain the process of photosynthesis in simple terms without using complex biological jargon. This explanation should be understandable for someone who has no background in biology.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nImagine the plants in your garden as tiny chefs. Their main ingredient to cook food is sunlight. They catch the sunlight using a green substance in their leaves called chlorophyll. To start cooking, they also need water, which they suck up from the ground through their roots. They add in some carbon dioxide as seasoning, which they pull in from the air through small holes in their leaves. With these ingredients and the energy from the sunlight, they whip up their own food, a type of sugar called glucose. As a bonus, they also produce oxygen, which they give back to the environment.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nPhotosynthesis is a process that plants use to make their own food. Here's how it works in simple terms:\n\n1. It all starts with the sun. The sun shines on the leaves of the plant. The leaves have a green substance called chlorophyll, which helps capture the sunlight.\n\n2. Once the sunlight is captured, the plant uses it as energy to start a chemical reaction.\n\n3. This reaction also needs water. The plant absorbs wate