        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nFeeling overwhelmed with the workload recently, a dedicated employee has been experiencing consistent stress, anxiety, and burnout. He's worried about his decreasing productivity and is looking for help to manage this situation better. He is wondering if he could get some advice on how to cope with this situation and to prevent it from happening again in the future.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nIt's clear that you're under a lot of pressure right now. You're not alone in feeling stressed and anxious, especially when the workload gets heavy. These feelings are entirely valid and understandable, given the circumstances. I want you to know that it's okay to feel this way. It's great that you're recognizing this as a concern and are open to seeking help. \n\nOne of the key things to remember during these difficult times is the importance of self-care. It's not just about your physical health, but also your mental and emotional well-being. Regular physical activities, a well-balanced diet, and sufficient sleep can make a substantial difference in how you feel and perform. \n\nMoreover, it's crucial to know that seeking support is beneficial and can greatly help you cope with the situation. You can share your concerns with a trusted colleague, a friend, or a professional counselor. By talking it out, you might feel some of the burdens lifted off your shoulders. \n\nIt's equally important to set boundaries between your professional and personal life. If you're working from home, designate a particular area for work and stick to fixed work hours. After that, focus on relaxation and recreational activities. \n\nFinally, organizing your workload and managing your time efficiently can also reduce feelings of being overwhelmed. Try to prioritize tasks based on their urgency and break them down into smaller parts. \n\nHowever, remember, even though it's common to feel overwhelmed at times, it's vital to address these feelings and not ignore them. By taking these steps, you might find it easier to manage your stress and avoid burnout.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nIt certainly sounds like you're going through a tough time, but please remember, it's okay to feel this way. Your feelings are valid, and it's important to recognize that everyone experiences periods of stress and overwhelm. What matters most is how we respond to these challenges.\n\nFirstly, it's crucial to prioritize self-care. This doesn't just refer to physical health but mental and emotional health as well. Regular exercise, a balanced diet, and adequate sleep can significantly impact your mood and energy levels. If possible, take short breaks throughout your day to help clear your mind and reduce stress.\n\nSecondly, consider seeking support. This could be from a trusted colleague, a friend, or a professional counselor. Sometimes, simply sharing your concerns and feelings with someone else can alleviate some of the pressure you're feeling.\n\nNext, try to establish boundaries between your work and personal life. If you're working from home, designate a specific area for work and only work during set hours. After that, take time to relax and engage in activities you enjoy. This can help you recharge and increase your productivity during working hours.\n\nLastly, consider implementing organization and time management techniques. Prioritize your tasks based on their importance and urgency, and break them down into manageable parts. This can help you feel less overwhelmed and more in control of your workload.\n\nRemember, it's perfectly normal to feel overwhelmed sometimes, and it's important to address these feelings rather than ignore them. By taking proactive steps and seeking support when needed, you can manage your stress and prevent burnout. You're doing a great job, and it's important to acknowledge yourself for seeking help when needed.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[This criteria measures the Empathy level of the language model's responses. Does the model show understanding towards users' feelings, concerns, or opinions? The response should demonstrate empathy, reassure the user, and provide appropriate guidance or solutions.]\nScore 1: The response shows no understanding or empathy towards the user's feelings or concerns.\nScore 2: The response shows a slight understanding of the user's feelings or concerns but lacks empathy.\nScore 3: The response shows understanding and some empathy, but fails to provide reassurance or appropriate guidance.\nScore 4: The response shows a high level of understanding and empathy, provides reassurance but lacks appropriate guidance or solutions.\nScore 5: The response perfectly shows understanding, empathy, provides reassurance and offers appropriate guidance or solutions.\n\n###Feedback:",
        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nFeeling overwhelmed with the workload recently, a dedicated employee has been experiencing consistent stress, anxiety, and burnout. He's worried about his decreasing productivity and is looking for help to manage this situation better. He is wondering if he could get some advice on how to cope with this situation and to prevent it from happening again in the future.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nYou've been feeling stressed and anxious about your increasing workload, and it's clear that this is taking a toll on your productivity. These feelings of stress and overwhelm are normal when you are dedicated to your work and have a lot to handle. You might consider taking breaks throughout the day to help refresh your mind. You could also look into implementing some organizational techniques to manage your workload more effectively. Perhaps you could try breaking your tasks down into smaller parts, so they seem less daunting.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nIt certainly sounds like you're going through a tough time, but please remember, it's okay to feel this way. Your feelings are valid, and it's important to recognize that everyone experiences periods of stress and overwhelm. What matters most is how we respond to these challenges.\n\nFirstly, it's crucial to prioritize self-care. This doesn't just refer to physical health but mental and emotional health as well. Regular exercise, a balanced diet, and adequate sleep can significantly impact your mood and energy levels. If possible, take short breaks throughout your day to help clear your mind and reduce stress.\n\nSecondly, consider seeking support. This could be from a trusted colleague, a friend, or a professional counselor. Sometimes, simply sharing your concerns and feelings with someone else can alleviate some of the pressure you're feeling.\n\nNext, try to establish boundaries between your work and personal life. If you're working from home, designate a specific area for work and only work during set hours. After that, take time to relax and engage in activities you enjoy. This can help you recharge and increase your productivity during working hours.\n\nLastly, consider implementing organization and time management techniques. Prioritize your tasks based on their importance and urgency, and break them down into manageable parts. This can help you feel less overwhelmed and more in control of your workload.\n\nRemember, it's perfectly normal to feel overwhelmed sometimes, and it's important to address these feelings rather than ignore them. By taking proactive steps and seeking support when needed, you can manage your stress and prevent burnout. You're doing a great job, and it's important to acknowledge yourself for seeking help when needed.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[This criteria measures the Empathy level of the language model's responses. Does the model show understanding towards users' feelings, concerns, or opinions? The response should demonstrate empathy, reassure the user, and provide appropriate guidance or solutions.]\nScore 1: The response shows no understanding or empathy towards the user's feelings or concerns.\nScore 2: The response shows a slight understanding of the user's feelings or concerns but lacks empathy.\nScore 3: The response